TASK 12 – Re-evaluate and Adapt the Design (8 Marks)
A. Impact Analysis – 2 Marks
The original parking system supported bikes, cars and electric cars with 3 floors. The new requirements introduce:
•	Two new vehicle categories: E-Bike and Delivery Van.
•	E-Bikes have a fixed flat parking fee.
•	Delivery Vans are charged at double the car rate between 9 AM and 5 PM.
•	Visitors can purchase a one-day parking pass.
•	The parking facility is extended to 5 floors, with different slot counts on each floor.
Affected classes and data structures:
1.	Vehicle, ParkingFacility, and ParkingTicket need modifications.
2.	New subclasses EBike and DeliveryVan are required.
3.	Pricing logic must support different vehicle rates and time-based charges.
4.	The original rectangular 2D array is unsuitable because every floor has a different number of slots. A jagged array is required.
Example:
String[][] slots = {
    new String[10],
    new String[15],
    new String[8],
    new String[12],
    new String[20]
};
Existing classes such as Car and TwoWheeler can remain unchanged if the new pricing rules are handled separately.
B. Evaluation of the Original Design – 2 Marks
The original design uses inheritance, method overriding and interfaces. It is suitable for adding new vehicle types because new subclasses can be created without rewriting existing vehicle classes.
However, placing all pricing conditions inside individual vehicle classes can make future changes difficult. For example, delivery van charges depend on the parking time.
Therefore, a separate PricingRule abstraction is better because all pricing rules can be maintained in one place.
The existing tested classes can mostly remain unchanged. Only the parking facility, ticket handling and pricing-related design need modification.
C. Adaptation or Redesign – 2 Marks
Decision: MODIFY the original design.
The revised design uses inheritance, interfaces, a pricing abstraction and a jagged array.
Revised class structure:
              Vehicle (Abstract)
                    |
       ----------------------------
       |          |       |       |
   TwoWheeler    Car   EBike  DeliveryVan
                    |
                ElectricCar

        PricingRule (Interface)
                 |
          ParkingPricing

          Pass (Interface)
                 |
            OneDayPass

          ParkingFacility
                 |
          Jagged Array
Java implementation:
import java.time.LocalTime;
abstract class Vehicle {
    String regNo;

    Vehicle(String regNo) {
        this.regNo = regNo;
    }
}
class Car extends Vehicle {
    Car(String regNo) {
        super(regNo);
    }
}
class EBike extends Vehicle {
    EBike(String regNo) {
        super(regNo);
    }
}

class DeliveryVan extends Vehicle {
    DeliveryVan(String regNo) {
        super(regNo);
    }
}
interface PricingRule {
    double calculateFee(Vehicle v, int hours, LocalTime time);
}
class ParkingPricing implements PricingRule {
    public double calculateFee(
        Vehicle v, int hours, LocalTime time) {
        if (v instanceof EBike)
            return 20; // Flat fee
        if (v instanceof DeliveryVan) {
            double rate = 30;
            if (!time.isBefore(LocalTime.of(9, 0)) &&
                time.isBefore(LocalTime.of(17, 0))) {
                rate = rate * 2;
            }
            return rate * hours;
        }
        if (v instanceof Car)
            return 30 * hours;
        return 10 * hours;
    }
}
interface Pass {
    boolean isValid();
}

class OneDayPass implements Pass {
    public boolean isValid() {
        return true;
    }
    double getFee() {
        return 100;
    }
}
class ParkingFacility {
    String[][] slots = {
        new String[10],
        new String[15],
        new String[8],
        new String[12],
        new String[20]
    };
    void displayFloors() {
        for (int i = 0; i < slots.length; i++) {
            System.out.println(
                "Floor " + (i + 1) +
                " Slots: " + slots[i].length);
        }
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ParkingPricing pricing = new ParkingPricing();
        System.out.println("E-Bike Fee: " +
            pricing.calculateFee(
                new EBike("EB101"), 3,
                LocalTime.of(10, 0)));

        System.out.println("Delivery Van Fee: " +
            pricing.calculateFee(
                new DeliveryVan("DV101"), 2,
                LocalTime.of(10, 0)));
        OneDayPass pass = new OneDayPass();
        System.out.println("One Day Pass Fee: " +
            pass.getFee());
        ParkingFacility parking = new ParkingFacility();
        parking.displayFloors();
    }
}
